---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { THEME_STORAGE_KEY } from "../lib/theme-key";
import { PALETTE_STORAGE_KEY } from "../lib/palette-key";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What ui.half-built-robots.com collects, what it keeps in the browser, and who to contact."
>
  <main>
    <article class="static-page bracket-frame">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Last updated: September 29, 2026</p>
        <p>
          This policy covers ui.half-built-robots.com, the reference site for
          the @half-built packages. The site is owned by Curt Henrichs LLC, a
          California LLC. It is a static site with no accounts, forms, comments,
          or ads, and it collects almost nothing.
        </p>

        <h2>What the site collects</h2>
        <p>
          The site is hosted by
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/">Cloudflare</a>. Like nearly
          every host, Cloudflare may keep standard request logs (IP address,
          browser type, and the pages requested) as part of serving the site.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site uses
          <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/"
            >Cloudflare Web Analytics</a
          >
          to count page views. Cloudflare adds a small script to each page for
          this. It sets no cookies, stores nothing in the browser, and does not
          follow visitors to other sites. The result is a tally of which pages
          were viewed.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
        <p>
          The site sets no cookies of its own. Cloudflare runs bot protection in
          front of the site, and that sets one cookie, <code>cf_clearance</code
          >. It records that the browser already passed Cloudflare's check, so
          it is not challenged again. It lasts up to a year, only Cloudflare can
          read it, and it is not used for ads or cross-site tracking.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site also keeps a few small values in the browser's local storage.
          None of it is sent anywhere and none of it identifies anyone.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <code>{THEME_STORAGE_KEY}</code>: the light or dark mode choice,
            saved when the theme toggle is used.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>{PALETTE_STORAGE_KEY}</code>: the colors picked in the palette
            editor, saved so the page keeps them on reload.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>half-built-ecosystem</code>: a copy of the footer's list of
            related sites, kept for a day so it is not fetched on every page.
            The list comes from ecosystem.half-built-robots.com, which is also
            run by Curt Henrichs LLC on Cloudflare.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>Clearing the browser's data for this site removes all of it.</p>

        <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing on this site tracks visitors across other sites, so it behaves
          the same whether or not the browser sends a Do Not Track or Global
          Privacy Control signal. There is nothing for the signal to turn off.
        </p>

        <h2>Why it is kept and for how long</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Cloudflare's logs, analytics, and bot protection.</strong>
            These keep the site running and protected. Cloudflare keeps them on
            its own schedule under
            <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
              >Cloudflare's privacy policy</a
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Email sent to the contact address.</strong> It is used to
            answer the sender, and it is kept unless the sender asks for it to
            be deleted.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Where it is processed</h2>
        <p>
          Cloudflare and Google are United States companies, so anything they
          hold for this site is processed in the US. Cloudflare takes part in
          the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.
        </p>

        <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          The site links to GitHub, npm, and Half-Built Robots. Their privacy
          practices are their own; this policy covers only this site.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          This site is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly
          collect personal information from anyone under 13.
        </p>

        <h2>Your data</h2>
        <p>
          Anyone, wherever they live, can ask what this site holds about them.
          They can also ask to have it corrected, deleted, or sent to them as a
          copy, or ask for it not to be used. Write to the address below. The
          site itself holds nothing about its visitors, so the answer is almost
          always nothing.
        </p>
        <p>
          Anyone who thinks a request was handled badly can complain to the data
          protection authority where they live.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          Updates to this policy are posted on this page with a new date at the
          top.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Email:
            <a href="mailto:curthenrichs@gmail.com">curthenrichs@gmail.com</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            X/Twitter: <a href="https://x.com/curt_henrichs">@curt_henrichs</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            Bluesky:
            <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/curt-henrichs.bsky.social"
              >@curt-henrichs.bsky.social</a
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The email address is a Gmail account, so mail sent to it is also
          handled by Google under
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            >Google's privacy policy</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
